 "_doc": "Site 1 item 26, stretch 1, survey 1.07-1.14: the Bar Harbor Regency's pier and floats. Level metres. Pier: traced on the raw lidar (ME_MidCoast 2021, tide -1.33): deck +3.92, rails +5.05, lamps +6.6, 48 x 3.6 m, its line 37.8 deg, not the +5.0 the survey first said (that was the rail). Built of: from marinas.com's undated aerials (before 2022: the truss bridges still stand), read as a small bridge on concrete portal bents, ASSUMED concrete and steel girders; bents at 10, 20.5, 31.6, 42 m from the top-down photo, scaled on the lidar's 48 m (11.2 px/m). Floats: absent from the lidar, so summer only. Gangway 9.5 m; stem 74 m with the photo's joints (21.4, 12.5, 40.2), the T head from chart SLCONS 544 and OSM 693638909 and the resort's own page ('T-shaped floating dock 200 feet in length and 140 feet across the top'): the T head is NOT in the aerials, so it came later. The comb and the small float at the stem's root are in the aerials; the small float is on the chart, the comb is not, so the comb is ASSUMED still there until V1.1.",
